  "_garments": "A look with a 'garment' wears one of Status Wear's long garments in place of the outfit's body and trousers: a robe (clergy, herbalists, elders), a gown (noblewomen and well-to-do women: ladies, queens, stewards, merchants) or a coat (their menfolk: lords, stewards, merchants, kings; over plain trousers and the ranger's boots). It is described with its dye.",
  "garment_describe": { "robe": "a long %s wool robe with wide sleeves and a cord girdle", "gown": "a floor-length %s gown with wide sleeves and a gold girdle", "coat": "a knee-length %s coat edged in gold braid, belted" }
